---
description: Forbid getattr/hasattr and AttributeError masking; prefer DI and dataclasses
globs: "**/*.py"
alwaysApply: true
---

# No dynamic attribute access

Do not use dynamic access to paper over a missing contract.

## Forbidden

- `getattr(...)`, `hasattr(...)` to choose a business implementation or optional collaborator
- `except AttributeError` to compensate for an incomplete fake or API
- `object.__setattr__(...)` / `setattr(...)` (including frozen-dataclass list copies)
- Owned `collections.namedtuple` / `typing.NamedTuple` / positional tuple value objects — use a `dataclass`

## Prefer

- Constructor injection and typed ports (`Protocol` / ABC)
- Complete fakes under `**/tests/fakes/`
- `isinstance(...)` against a known type when discrimination is required
- Explicit properties / fields instead of duck-typing
- Frozen snapshots with collection fields: use `tuple[T, ...]` (no `__post_init__` setattr)

## Rare exemption

```python
# solid-getattr: <reason>
```

on the same line or the line above the call.
